---
import ViralContacts from '../../components/ViralContacts.astro'
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { href } from '../../lib/site.ts'
---

<Layout title="SARS-CoV-2 contacts" description="SARS-CoV-2 proteins touching human disease proteins in PDB entries, with the ClinVar variants on the contact.">
  <article class="post">
    <p><a href={href('blog/2026-11-12-sars-cov-2/')}>← Where SARS-CoV-2 holds a human disease protein</a></p>
    <h1>SARS-CoV-2 contacts</h1>
    <p>
      Hover a residue count for the positions. A gene with no page of its own has no
      confident AlphaFold DB partner; it is here on experiment alone.
    </p>
    <p>
      The viral side is numbered within the mature protein, so the protease residues
      are the H41 and C145 that papers name. Hover the column for the precursor
      numbering, which for spike is the S numbering that lineage-defining
      substitutions are quoted in.
    </p>
    <ViralContacts />
  </article>
</Layout>
